{"version":"1.168.0","results":[{"check_id":"ssc-962bf4cc-ce7f-4433-a01b-abca7dd5219e","path":"requirements.pinned.txt","start":{"line":7,"col":1,"offset":0},"end":{"line":7,"col":1,"offset":0},"extra":{"metavars":{},"message":"Affected versions of filelock are vulnerable to Concurrent Execution using Shared Resource with Improper Synchronization ('Race Condition') / Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following') / Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition. filelock's SoftFileLock acquires locks by creating the lock file after a separate writability check, with no protection against symlinks. A local attacker who can write to the lock-file directory can plant a symlink in the window between the check and os.open(), redirecting the lock operation to an attacker-controlled file. This causes silent lock-acquisition failures, denial of service, or writes to unintended files. The soft lock is used directly, as the FileLock fallback when fcntl is unavailable, and on platforms lacking os.O_NOFOLLOW.","metadata":{"confidence":"HIGH","category":"security","cve":"CVE-2026-22701","cwe":["CWE-362: Concurrent Execution using Shared Resource with Improper Synchronization ('Race Condition')","CWE-367: Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition","CWE-59: Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following')"],"ghsa":"GHSA-qmgc-5h2g-mvrw","owasp":["A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components"],"publish-date":"2026-01-13T18:44:55Z","references":["https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qmgc-5h2g-mvrw","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-22701"],"release":"ga","sca-fix-versions":[{"filelock":"3.20.3"}],"sca-kind":"reachable","sca-schema":20230302,"sca-severity":"MODERATE","sca-vuln-database-identifier":"CVE-2026-22701","technology":["python"],"license":"Semgrep Rules License v1.0. For more details, visit semgrep.dev/legal/rules-license","vulnerability_class":["Other"],"sem